update modules set pip_name = $t$plr-ivoryos==1.0.0b3$t$, module_name = $t$OT2$t$, module_path = $t$plr_ivoryos.opentrons$t$, init_args = $j$[{"name": "simulated", "type": "bool", "default": true}, {"name": "host", "type": "str"}, {"name": "port", "type": "int", "default": 31950}, {"name": "worktable", "type": "str", "default": "worktable.json"}, {"name": "step_delay_s", "type": "float", "default": 0}]$j$::jsonb, schema = (select s->$t$OT2$t$ from _schemas), schema_source = 'introspection', updated_at = now(), description = $t$An Opentrons OT-2 through PyLabRobot 1.0. The robot is one instrument and each mounted pipette another (ot2_left, ot2_right), each with PyLabRobot's own steps; wells are written as PyLabRobot writes them (assay_plate[A1:H1]). What is mounted and what sits where is the worktable file. Simulated (the default) runs PyLabRobot's OT-2 against a simulated robot-server, since PyLabRobot has none for its 1.0 class: for a real robot, untick simulated and give host. Beta: pinned to PyLabRobot 1.0.0b1, run in simulation only. Decks on one computer share one Python environment, so this replaces the PyLabRobot that any older plr-ivoryos driver there needs. Add the Labware plugin after this driver to see and edit the worktable.$t$ where id = 183;

