update modules set pip_name = $t$plr-ivoryos==1.0.0b3$t$, module_name = $t$Nimbus$t$, module_path = $t$plr_ivoryos.legacy$t$, init_args = $j$[{"name": "simulated", "type": "bool", "default": true}, {"name": "host", "type": "str"}, {"name": "port", "type": "int", "default": 2000}, {"name": "worktable", "type": "str", "default": "worktable.json"}, {"name": "channels", "type": "int", "default": 8}, {"name": "step_delay_s", "type": "float", "default": 0}]$j$::jsonb, schema = (select s->$t$Nimbus$t$ from _schemas), schema_source = 'introspection', updated_at = now(), description = $t$A Hamilton Nimbus through PyLabRobot. PyLabRobot 1.0 drives this robot only through pylabrobot.legacy, so it is one instrument with every LiquidHandler operation (pick_up_tips, aspirate, dispense, move_plate, ...), PyLabRobot's names and arguments; wells are written as PyLabRobot writes them (assay_plate[A1:H1]). Simulated (the default) is PyLabRobot's legacy chatterbox: its tip and volume tracking, not the robot's firmware. Beta: pinned to PyLabRobot 1.0.0b1, run in simulation only. For a real Nimbus, untick simulated and give host. Decks on one computer share one Python environment, so this replaces the PyLabRobot that any older plr-ivoryos driver there needs. Add the Labware plugin after this driver to see and edit the worktable.$t$ where id = 184;

